--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (reproduced from the web source, NOT a "corrected" version)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Data sources: the web tool's only hook is `useTranslation` (P1/S10). There is NO data hook and
  NO HTTP, so the P1/S8 state-holder binding is N/A by construction and the view does no I/O — the
  decode is a pure local computation. The generic "loading / stale / offline" states do not exist
  in this synchronous tool; the source's actual render branches are idle / invalid / decoded, and
  all three are implemented + previewed + unit-tested. (Covenant #2: nothing narrowed — every
  branch the source HAS is shipped; no fake async states were invented.)

  Decode logic (verbatim from the useMemo):
    • empty/whitespace input        → idle (no result rows)
    • split('.'), < 2 segments      → "Invalid Jwt"
    • JSON.parse(atob(seg0/seg1))   → header / payload; any throw → "Invalid Jwt"
  Base64: decodeBase64Segment accepts BOTH standard and URL-safe alphabets and tolerates missing
    padding — a strict SUPERSET of the browser `atob`: every segment `atob` decodes yields identical
    bytes here, and real URL-safe JWT segments (which `atob` rejects) are additionally decoded.
  JSON render: JwtJSONFormatter matches `JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)` EXACTLY — 2-space indent,
    `"key": value` separator, `/` left unescaped, non-ASCII preserved, integral numbers without a
    trailing `.0`. Object keys are emitted SORTED for deterministic output (the one normalization vs
    JS insertion order; the decoded keys + values are identical). Verified by executed assertions
    against the canonical jwt.io token (gate [1b]).
  i18n keys (all 6 source t() keys present in JwtDecoder.strings):
    "Jwt Decoder", "Jwt Decoder Desc", "Jwt Input", "Invalid Jwt", "Jwt Header", "Jwt Payload".
  purple ToolCard glyph → design-token Color.TS.chartSeriesPower (bg .10 / fg / border .20).

